    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "TOM MAHER & COMPANY SCSI RICS IPAV - DEVELOPMENT POTENTIAL - This is a charming 3 bed semi-detached SOUTH-WEST facing cottage built circa 1932 situated on over c .39 acre / .16 hectares, the site is mainly regular in shape and enjoys panoramic un-spoilt views of the Dublin mountains, tremendous DEVELOPMENT POTENTIAL subject to the customary planning consents. Excellent road frontage onto the Old Court Road, vehicular access from the cul de sac, pedestrian access from the main Road. The property enjoys light-filled accommodation, surrounded by neatly manicured, mature extensive grounds.\r\n\r\nThis fine property is located opposite Ferncourt at the foothills of the Dublin Mountains, within a small mature enclave of homes that rarely come to the market. Old Bawn, Woodstown, Knocklyon and Rathfarnham shopping centres are literally on your doorstep. Dodder, Marley & St. Enda's Parks are also close by. A perfect setting for all families. The M50 motorway network, the N81 and N7 provide ease of access to various routes, circa 12k Dublin City Centre.\r\n\r\nThis property is sure to appeal to a wide range of discerning prospective buyers to include:\r\n-  The perfect property for those seeking a home with a large garden that has the potential to extend the existing accommodation\r\n-  Those that require a residential home with the added potential to create a separate dwelling/ modular home (s) on the site.\r\n-   Builders / Developers who wish to maximise the potential the land.\r\n-   Potential to add a workshop / excellent off-road parking\r\n-   To re-model and extend the existing\r\n\r\nThere are a wide range of parameters for this unrivalled property (subject to customary planning consents) REGISTER YOUR INTEREST BY EMAIL"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "Entrance rear hallway 2\r\nLounge : 4.66m x 3.38m feature slate fireplace, ceiling clad with wood\r\nKitchen/ Dining room : Solid Oak kitchen units and presses, tiled splash area\r\nShower room : 2.24m x 1.96m oversized shower cubicle with Triton T90sr electric shower - whb with storage - wc - The floor and wall areas are fully tiled.\r\nBedroom 1 : 2.46m x 4.53m wall-to- wall built in wardrobes incorporating vanity unit\r\nFront door hallway :  2.32m x .89m \r\nBedroom 2 : 2.84m x 2.02m \r\nBedroom 3 : 2.40m x 3.62m"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "PVC Doube-glazed windows throughout\r\nPart PVC fascia and soffit\r\nOil central heating upgraded boiler /  PVC tank\r\nTrip switch fuse board\r\nThe attic remains untouched\r\nAll mains services are laid on\r\nThe ceilings in the original house are almost 9ft \r\nThe kitchen and bathroom have mineral felt roof areas, replaced in the last 6 years\r\nThe boundary is mature hedging\r\nBlock garden shed / boiler house"
      },
